Revision history for Database-BI

0.018.0	Wed Oct 28 08:41:28 PM EDT 2026
	[ Enhancements ]
	- Cross-row columns: cs=<col>:<fn>:<alias>[:<arg>] with by= and order=
	  adds a running total, moving average, rank, z-score or share of the
	  total per row.  A Cross-row panel builds them; charts and exports
	  carry the new column.
	- Canvas cards can carry their own cross-row plan (cross_row), replacing
	  the page's, run on the card's own filtered rows.  Add current view
	  collects several columns; the card header's Edit cross-row edits the
	  plan as chips and warns when a rename affects a plotted column.
	  PATCH /api/analyses/:id/visuals/:visual replaces a card's plan.
	- Word cloud (GET /wordcloud, and canvas cards with kind=wordcloud),
	  drawn with HTML::TagCloud.  Each word links to its rows, or on a
	  canvas cross-filters to them.
	- Relative time ranges: ?range=<name>&rcol=<column> on every data route
	  and saved canvas (last_24_hours, today, yesterday, last_7_days,
	  last_30_days, last_90_days, this_month, last_month, this_quarter,
	  last_quarter, this_year, last_year).  An unknown name or missing rcol=
	  is a 400.  The dashboard filter bar and canvas toolbar have a Time
	  range menu.
	- The filter UI adapts to the column's detected type: date pickers,
	  numeric operators, or string operators.
	- New "between" filter operator (col:between:YYYY-MM-DD:YYYY-MM-DD);
	  lt/le/gt/ge compare ISO dates as dates.
	- New measures for the pivot, column statistics and canvas cards:
	  median, stdev, first, last, range and p<N> percentiles.
	- Time buckets: span= groups a chart or pivot by hour, day, week, month,
	  quarter or year; /graph?agg= plots one point per bucket.
	- Stored time patterns accept time=, e.g. 27/10/2026 14:05.
	- bi-alert: --suppress, --recovery (exit 3), --notify-cmd, and several
	  analyses and thresholds in one run.
	- Response compression, ETag/304 and HTML minification via
	  Mojolicious::Plugin::Buffer (new prerequisite); downloads opt out.
	- Optional page cache: page_cache_dir and page_cache_duration store
	  /catalog and /tutorial in a CHI File cache.
	- Internal: every data route's filter stage is one function,
	  _reduce_records.
	- Main navigation links to Canvases, Catalog and Open file on every page.
	- Chart, pivot, stats and insights pages show a "Drawn from:" strip naming
	  the time range, filters, cross-row columns, combined files and
	  de-duplication, with a link back to change them.
	- Every page has a full breadcrumb, from Home to the page itself, each
	  step named after what it shows: Home > sales > Bar chart: amount by
	  region > sales (region = East) > Pie chart: Count by region.  The
	  trail is read from each page's back links, so it is no longer cut at
	  two levels; a file opened from the browser sits under its folder, and
	  a canvas is named.  Back links to another site are not followed, and
	  the trail is at most eight steps.
	[ Bug Fixes ]
	- Two charts on one canvas no longer collide; the second card draws.
	- A card's cross-row column no longer appears in the cards beside it.
	- A card naming a column no plan produces is refused, instead of
	  printing a heading over empty cells.
	- A day bound on a timestamp column (e.g. le 2026-10-27) now includes
	  the rows stamped on that day.
	- A stale ?dd= bookmark no longer makes canvas marks unfocusable.
	- Canvas help now describes what the page actually does.
	- Charts, pivots, stats and insights of a combined (c=), de-duplicated
	  (d=1) or inner/outer-joined (jtype=) view now draw from the rows the
	  table shows; before, the panels dropped those parameters, and d=1 was
	  ignored by every chart route.  Export keeps jtype= too.
	- Opening any toolbar panel closes all the others: the histogram panel
	  left Cross-row and Word cloud open, and Merge, Combine and Export left
	  chart panels open and their own buttons disabled.
	- The Word cloud, Cross-row and Ask toolbar buttons are styled like the
	  others; all of them now share one btn-tool class.
	- Toolbar and filter-bar controls on the same row now line up top and
	  bottom: they share one height and are centred, rather than aligned on
	  their text baselines.
	- The pivot panel's Limit to top, ranked by, Time bucket and "of column"
	  fields are the same size as its Row, Column and Measure fields.
	- Canvas controls line up: the Time range bar, parameter bar and toolbar
	  share the table toolbar's height, the Time range menus and Apply
	  button are styled, and card-header buttons are one height.
	- Every dropdown and text field is white with one border colour, from a
	  single rule in the layout; the table page's filter bar and pivot fields
	  showed the browser's grey, and pivot fields turned near-black when the
	  OS was in dark mode.
	- An unknown canvas (/a/<id>) is an HTML page with the breadcrumb and
	  navigation, not a line of plain text.
	- Folder view levels keep the link back to the table they came from,
	  and its crumb is an absolute link.
	- A missing page is a 404 with the breadcrumb and navigation, not
	  Mojolicious's bare page.  /view/<table> for a table that does not
	  exist is now a 404 naming it, rather than the home page with an
	  error that showed the data directory.
	- A view that is both joined (j=) and combined (c=) shows both, from
	  /join or /combine: /combine ignored j=, and Merge after Combine
	  dropped c=.  The table now shows the rows its charts draw from.
	- Tests: the read-only model_dir and export-write-failure tests skip
	  where chmod cannot revoke access (Cygwin, Windows ACLs, root), using
	  Test::Permissions; they failed on Cygwin (CPAN Testers).
	  Fixes https://www.cpantesters.org/cpan/report/b2c11820-d297-11f1-a488-efeb21b3859a
	- Tests: t/unit.t no longer segfaults at exit under Devel::Cover on
	  perl 5.42 (the CI coverage step); its LLM-response helper was a
	  lexical "my sub".
	- Text::CSV is a prerequisite: script/bi-alert's fallback reader needed
	  it and it was not declared.
	- Documentation: cross-row columns (cs=, by=, order=), compression and the
	  page cache (page_cache_dir, page_cache_duration), breadcrumbs and 404
	  pages, j= with c= on /join and /combine, and an API SPECIFICATION for
	  every public function.  Util.pm's licence now matches the
	  distribution's (GPL2).  Fixed POD that rendered "= >" and "&>".
	- The templates and controller comments are ASCII again.

0.017.1	Sun Oct 25 09:23:34 PM EDT 2026
	[ Bug Fixes ]
	- script/database-bi: shebang is perl again; the script starts morbo
	  itself when given no arguments.  0.017.0's morbo shebang caused each
	  worker to spawn another morbo, growing PERL5LIB until exec failed with
	  E2BIG.
	- GET /map: HTML::OSM older than 0.12 now produces a warning page instead
	  of a 500.  0.017.0 passed search => 0 and max_zoom unconditionally;
	  older HTML::OSM rejected the unknown keys.
	- GET /map: ?agg= removed (it was accepted and ignored).
	- /join: schema-type mismatch warnings now fire correctly.  DataSource
	  delegates schema() to its inner backend; the controller compares types
	  across join steps and reports differing columns.
	- data_dir may be absolute.  A relative value is still resolved against
	  the application home; an absolute one was previously appended to it.
	- Database::BI::Extract: removed unused _get_or_build_extract; corrected
	  class docs (the web app does not materialise extracts).
	- script/bi-alert: corrected docs -- it writes to STDOUT, not email.
	  --dry-run is accepted for compatibility only.
	- Parallel test runs (HARNESS_OPTIONS=j10) are now deterministic.  Upload
	  staging moved to a per-deployment uploads_dir config key (.uploads by
	  default); test files each use their own temp directory.
	- Browser fixture: selector quoting no longer depends on the JSON
	  backend's allow_nonref setting.
	- t/integration.t: %INC restored after Test::Without::Module block,
	  eliminating "Subroutine ... redefined" noise.
	- Every page now sets <html lang> from the resolved language.  36 render
	  calls were missing the stash key.
	- Geo::Coder::Free minimum raised to 0.48 throughout (floor constant,
	  error messages, docs).  The floor was 0.47, but 0.48 introduced the
	  per-lookup read counts the application uses.
	- _resolve_language now falls back to the default language when the
	  resolved code has no template directory, as documented.
	[ New Features ]
	- GET /map: ?size=<col> draws bubble markers scaled 6-30 px.
	- GET /map: ?series=<col>&scheme=<name> colours markers by category with
	  a legend.  Mutually exclusive with ?color=.
	[ Documentation ]
	- Complete /map parameter reference; HTML::OSM 0.12 floor;
	  Nominatim search always suppressed.
	- "Command-line tools" section covering all three scripts.
	- Canvas, analyses API, sharing/embedding, catalog, insights, ask,
	  summary and geo endpoints (previously README-only).
	[ Tests ]
	- t/launcher.t: asserts perl shebang on every shipped script.
	- t/map.t and t/integration.t: drive both renderer states via the
	  controller's _map_renderer_version probe.
	- t/edge_cases.t: covers uploads_dir resolution (absolute, relative, unset).
	- t/map.t: covers the canvas in both renderer states.
	- Every test file now gives the app its own model_dir temp directory.
	- t/browser-canvas-map-degraded.t: browser test for the degraded map card.
	- Map-rendering assertions in t/map.t, t/integration.t and t/unit.t now
	  require HTML::OSM 0.12 (not merely installed).
	- browser.yml: no-renderer, no-renderer-canvas, no-geocoder and renderer
	  jobs added; each pins or verifies one optional module.
	- BI::Test::Browser: config keys written before app startup; fixture
	  builds a language home for non-shipped locales; app_setup coderef
	  supported.
	- t/browser-fixture.t: checks fixture behaviour without a browser.
	- t/browser-map-page-renderer.t, t/browser-map-geocoder.t,
	  t/browser-canvas-map-geocoder.t: browser coverage for optional-module
	  degraded states.
	- t/browser-offline-assets.t: skips map assertions below HTML::OSM 0.12;
	  adds D3-drawn bar assertions.
	- t/recommended-versions.t: asserts tests and application code gate
	  recommended modules at the declared version floor.
	- t/browser-language.t: browser coverage for configured, default and
	  fallback languages.
	- .github/workflows/actionlint.yml: lints all workflows on push/PR
	  (pinned actionlint 1.7.12 + shellcheck 0.10.0); fixed 24 shellcheck
	  findings in existing workflows.
	- browser.yml: keyboard job handles missing HTML::OSM without failing;
	  browser-map-panel.t no longer dies when a card has no script.
	- Every browser job publishes a coverage report to the job summary.
	- t/workflow-browser.t: guards the renderer job's file list.

0.017.0	Sat Oct 24 06:12:53 PM EDT 2026
	[ New Features ]
	- GET /geo/list, POST /geo/save, POST /geo/delete: coordinate-column
	  preference CRUD.  Saves the user's choice of lat=, lon=, or loc=
	  column for a given l= spec in .bi/models.json under geo.<spec>.columns.
	  The Map panel now fetches /geo/list on open and pre-populates the
	  column selects from the saved preferences, falling back to the existing
	  name-heuristic when none are saved.  A "Remember columns" checkbox
	  fires POST /geo/save on form submit.
	- GET /map: new optional URL params.
	  ?zoom=N (0-19): passes an initial zoom level to HTML::OSM instead of
	    auto-fitting to the marker bounds.
	  ?tiles=name: selects a named tile source from the tile_sources config
	    key (unknown name returns 400).  Arbitrary URLs are never accepted.
	  ?heat=1: adds a Leaflet heatmap layer over the regular markers using
	    HTML::OSM->add_heatmap (present in HTML::OSM >= 0.11).
	  ?weight=<col>: numeric column that drives heatmap point intensity;
	    values are normalised to [0,1]; defaults to equal weight 1 when
	    absent.
	  ?max_zoom=N (0-28): sets the Leaflet tile layer maxZoom option so the
	    user cannot zoom past what the tile server covers.  Also readable
	    from the map_max_zoom config key; the URL param takes precedence.
	    Requires HTML::OSM >= 0.12.
	- GET /map: Nominatim live-search box is now suppressed (search => 0
	  passed to HTML::OSM).  The Reset Map button is retained; only the
	  search input and Nominatim egress are removed.  Requires HTML::OSM >=
	  0.12.
	- script/bi-geocode: new CLI warming script.
	  Opens a dataset spec, geocodes every distinct value of the named
	  column, and writes the resolved coordinates into the shared geocode
	  cache in .bi/models.json.  Idempotent: a second run against a warm
	  cache resolves zero places and writes nothing.  Suitable for cron.
	  Flags: --spec, --col, --data-dir, --model-dir, --openaddr, --region,
	  --dry-run, --verbose.
	[ Dependency changes ]
	- HTML::OSM minimum bumped from 0.11 to 0.12 (search => 0 and max_zoom
	  constructor params; tile_url was already present in 0.11).

0.016.0	Fri Oct 23 08:58:00 AM EDT 2026
	[ New Features ]
	- POST /api/ask: Natural language to analysis spec.
	  Translates a plain-English question into an analysis spec by
	  calling the Anthropic Messages API.  The model receives only column
	  names and types -- no raw row data, no file paths.  The returned spec
	  is validated (column names and kind checked) before being returned.
	  The feature is absent (503) when ai_api_key is not configured.
	  Database::BI::Ask -- new module.
	  Ask... button added to the dashboard toolbar when ai_api_key is set.
	  New test suite t/ask.t.
	- GET /insights: Automatic statistical insights panel.
	  Detects outliers (Tukey IQR fence), period-over-period deltas,
	  top movers by dimension, and seasonality (lag-1 autocorrelation
	  on monthly totals, threshold r>=0.6).  No LLM or external service
	  required.  Every insight includes a view_url linking to the chart
	  or stats page that shows the underlying data.
	  Database::BI::Insights -- new module; pure arithmetic, no eval.
	  New test suite t/insights.t (218 subtests).
	- Insights button added to the dashboard toolbar (next to Column stats).
	- POST /api/summary: Narrative summary generation.
	  Two paths: deterministic template sentences (offline, always available)
	  and optional LLM polish via the Anthropic Messages API (opt-in,
	  activated by setting ai_api_key in the app config and passing ai=1).
	  Only aggregate insight facts are sent to the LLM -- no raw row data,
	  no file paths.  Results are cached in-process for 1 hour.
	  Database::BI::Summary -- new module.
	  Summarize button added to /insights page; Use AI opt-in checkbox
	  shown when ai_api_key is configured in the app.
	  New test suite t/summary.t.
	  [ Bug Fixes ]
	  - Fixed https://matrix.perl-magpie.org/results/fbe5436e-cd3d-11f1-9632-bd4d6e8775ea

0.015.0 Tue Oct 20 08:10:43 PM EDT 2026
	[ New Features ]
	- GET /tutorial: in-application tutorial with a chapter for every page
	  feature (Database::BI::Tutorial).  Each chapter has numbered steps, a
	  tip, and a Try it link.  Chapters for joins, pivot, calc fields, canvas,
	  and five chart types include a worked walk-through.  F1 opens the chapter
	  for the current page; a "Help:" link in the header does the same.
	  t/tutorial.t enforces that every GET page has a chapter and no sentence
	  exceeds 25 words.
	- Dataset catalog (GET /catalog): lists all files in data_dir with type,
	  size, last-modified date, and which saved analyses reference each file.
	- Sharing and embedding: POST /api/analyses/:id/share issues a signed
	  HMAC token.  GET /share/:id?token= renders a read-only canvas;
	  GET /embed/:id?token= renders a chrome-less embed page.
	  GET /a/:id/visual/:n/csv downloads one visual's data as CSV.
	- Extract cache (Database::BI::Extract): query results are materialised as
	  SQLite files under model_dir/extracts/ keyed by source fingerprint.
	  Deleting the extracts/ directory leaves the app fully functional.
	- bi-alert CLI (script/bi-alert): evaluates a saved analysis against a
	  threshold (--threshold alias:op:value).  Exit 0 = ok, 1 = crossed,
	  2 = error.  Schedule via cron.
	[ Enhancements ]
	- Map markers cluster with Leaflet.markercluster: overlapping pins show a
	  count at low zoom and split into individual markers as you zoom in.
	- Geocode answers are now shared across all datasets in the model store.
	  A place is resolved once and any other dataset that names it plots it
	  immediately without another lookup.
	- D3, Leaflet, and tile-server URLs are all configurable, so a deployment
	  with no outbound network access can serve every asset itself.
	- Map is a canvas visual kind.  New Canvas and Add to Existing Canvas both
	  start from the map's lat/lon or geocoded column spec.  Canvas map cards
	  support in-place column editing without a page reload.
	- Add visual panel on canvas: append a table, chart, or map card to an
	  open canvas without leaving the page.
	- New Canvas seeds itself from the current table or chart, including its
	  kind, columns, and options, so a pie chart stays a pie on the canvas.
	- Multi-table SQLite files support a nested spec (table:store/customer).
	  The join and combine panels list each internal table separately.
	- Map marker popups now show all non-coordinate columns by default.
	  Pass ?popup=col to restrict the popup to specific columns.
	- data/virginia_counties.csv added: all 95 Virginia counties with 2020
	  census populations, lat/lon centroids, and region labels.  Tutorial
	  walk-throughs for map, pie, bar, scatter, and stats use this file.
	- Canvas home-page cards support Ctrl+click and rubber-band drag for
	  multi-select; a floating action bar offers bulk delete.
	- Canvas freshness banner warns when a source file has changed since the
	  analysis was last saved.
	[ Bug Fixes ]
	- Canvas treemap cards no longer return 500.
	- Chart options (orientation, max_items, show_values) are now preserved
	  when seeding a canvas from a chart page.
	- D3 is now loaded before chart cards, so inline chart scripts run
	  correctly on first render.
	- Cross-filtered canvas charts now aggregate the filtered rows, not the
	  full source.
	- Stored calc fields now appear in /view/:table (not only in chart views).

0.014.0	Mon Oct 19 09:49:36 AM EDT 2026
	[ New Features ]
	- GET /map renders the filtered dataset on an OpenStreetMap map via
	  HTML::OSM (optional).  Use lat=/lon= for coordinate columns already in
	  the data, or loc=<column> to geocode a place-name column.  Rows sharing
	  a position are collapsed to one marker; out-of-range coordinate columns
	  return 400; markers and popup columns are configurable.
	- Database::BI::Model::Geocode resolves place-name columns via
	  Geo::Coder::Free (optional, >= 0.47).  Lookups are one-per-distinct-value,
	  cached in the model store (.bi/models.json), capped per request
	  (map_geocode_max), and skipped rather than failed for blanks and bare
	  numbers.  Without the geocoder, previously resolved places are still
	  plotted.
	[ Enhancements ]
	- Full keyboard accessibility audit.  Canvas and chart resize handles are
	  now sliders in the tab order (arrow keys, Shift for bigger steps, Home/End
	  for min/max); card size can also be set from a Size menu on each card.
	  Canvas cards are draggable to a chosen grid cell from the keyboard
	  (arrow keys in the header, Shift+arrow for edge).  Pivot column headers
	  sort (Enter/Space) and move (Shift+Left/Right) from the keyboard.
	  Home-page card tooltips appear on focus.  Stacked and multi-series line
	  chart legends are toggle switches.  Treemap tile values are read in the
	  tile name.  Every size change and card move is announced via a live region.
	- Browser test suite (t/browser-*.t) driven by headless Firefox via
	  Marionette.  Covers canvas keyboard controls, chart resize/export/a11y,
	  pivot keyboard, and home-page focus behaviour.  Runs as a separate CI
	  job (.github/workflows/browser.yml); skips automatically when Firefox
	  is unavailable.
	[ Bug Fixes ]
	- GET /combo: ?bar_val= and ?line_val= are now the canonical parameter
	  names (?bar= and ?line= kept as aliases).  ?cat= is now the canonical
	  x-axis parameter (?x= kept as alias), consistent with /stacked.

0.013.0 Fri Oct 16 04:08:48 PM EDT 2026
	[ New Features ]
	- Saved canvases: multi-visual workspace pages (/a/:id) that combine
	  charts and table views.  Full CRUD API at /api/analyses.  Canvas
	  pages support cross-filtering, drill-through hierarchies,
	  parameterisation (?p.<name>=), bookmarks with undo/redo, per-visual
	  PNG download, and print to PDF/paper.
	[ Enhancements ]
	- Chart resize: all chart pages (line, pie, bar, heatmap, scatter,
	  stacked, combo, treemap, histogram) now show a drag handle at the
	  bottom-right corner of the chart SVG.  Dragging it resizes the chart
	  proportionally without a page reload or D3 re-render.

0.012.1	Thu Oct 15 12:00:00 PM EDT 2026
    [ Bug Fixes ]
    - Fix 'Argument "" isn't numeric in int' warnings logged to the console
      when numeric query parameters (?topn=, ?max=, ?max_cols=, ?per_page=,
      ?page=, ?min_r=, ?max_r=) are submitted with an empty value.
    - Fix ?bins=0 reverting to 10 bins instead of clamping to 1: the
      || 10 empty-string guard must not swallow the literal value 0.
      histogram_view now uses the defined-and-non-empty pattern so that
      ?bins=0 correctly passes through the $bins < 1 clamp.
    [ Tests ]
    - Add t/binned.t: end-to-end contract tests for /histogram pre-binned
      mode (label/count correctness, bins=N clamping, max-lands-in-top-bin,
      no d3.bin() call, bin()/histogram label agreement, virtual column
      binning, flat fixture, empty/error state).

0.012.0	Wed Oct 14 09:10:15 PM EDT 2026
    [ New Features ]
    - GET /pivot: crosstab/pivot table.  Accepts ?rows=, ?cols=, and
      ?m=col:fn:alias (sum|avg|min|max|count|count_distinct); ?totals=1
      adds subtotals and a grand-total row; ?h= applies post-aggregation
      HAVING filters; ?topn=N+?topn_col= keeps the top-N row groups;
      ?max_cols=N collapses tail column combos into "Other";
      ?format=csv|sqlite|json|xlsx exports the result.
    - GET /stats: per-column statistics (row count, null count, distinct
      count, min, max, mean, median).
    - GET /scatter: scatter/bubble plot (?x=, ?y=, ?series=, ?size=,
      ?scheme=, ?min_r=, ?max_r=).  The scatter panel now exposes all
      parameters: "Colour by" (any column), "Bubble size" (numeric
      columns only), colour scheme (tableau10|category10|set2|set3|paired
      -- enabled only when a series column is chosen), and Min/Max radius
      1-40 (enabled only when a size column is chosen).  ?scheme= is
      validated server-side; an unrecognised name returns 400.
    - GET /stacked: stacked bar chart (?cat=, ?series=, ?val=).
    - GET /combo: combo bar+line chart (?cat=, ?bar_val=, ?line_val=).
    - GET /treemap: treemap (?group=, ?size=, ?topn=N).
    - GET /histogram: histogram with server-side binning (?col=, ?bins=N;
      default 10 bins; max 200).
    - GET /line: alias for GET /graph (all /graph params accepted).
    - GET /graph: new ?series=<col> parameter for multi-series line charts.
    - Calculated fields (Database::BI::Calc): recursive-descent evaluator
      supporting arithmetic, comparison, IF, string, numeric, and date
      functions; bin(); coalesce; isnull.  All chart and pivot routes
      accept ?c=name:expr (repeatable).  Stored fields managed via
      GET /calc/list, POST /calc/save, POST /calc/delete.
    - Date normalisation: stored date-format patterns convert non-ISO
      columns to ISO-8601 before aggregation.  Managed via
      GET /dates/list, POST /dates/save, POST /dates/delete.
    - Named value groups: virtual "${col}_group" columns map raw values
      to analyst-defined labels.  Managed via GET /groups/list,
      POST /groups/save, POST /groups/delete.
    - Redis backend: DataSource accepts redis => 'redis://...' and the
      redis:tablename|redis://... spec format.

    [ Enhancements ]
    - GET /join and GET /combine now support pagination (?page=N,
      ?per_page=M, ?sort=<col>, ?dir=asc|desc).
    - GET /export and POST /export now accept ?page=N and ?per_page=M.
    - f= filters and d=1 dedup applied before pagination so the N+1
      row count reflects the reduced set (reduce-before-paginate).
    - bar_view and pie_view: new ?topn=N parameter; remainder collapsed
      into "Other".
    - Added X-BI-Warnings response header to GET /export.
    - All chart render() calls now use a unified chart_html stash key
      and include a chart => { kind, title, encode, options } DTO.
    - Added DataSource::dbi_source() for SQL-capability detection and
      Database::Join zero-copy ATTACH path.
    - Added _grouped_totals() as the single aggregation entry point for
      all chart routes, with SQL push-down and Perl fold fallback.

    [ Bug Fixes ]
    - /join and /combine: no-params default now returns the first 200
      rows with a pagination bar, consistent with /view and /open.
    - f= filters on paginated views no longer produce short pages.
    - d=1 dedup now deduplicates the full result before slicing.
    - has_next recomputed after in-memory filter/dedup reduction.
    - Chart category order no longer changes when a filter is applied:
      Perl fold now returns groups in the same ascending key order as
      the SQL path.
    - Aggregation on SQLite sources pushes SQL-compatible f= filters to
      the database; non-SQL-able filters still fall back to Perl fold.
    - DataSource::dbi_source() no longer propagates exceptions from
      non-SQL backends; returns undef instead.
    - CSV and other non-SQL sources no longer emit "Bad limit clause"
      warnings; LIMIT/OFFSET is only sent to SQL-backed sources.

    [ Dependencies ]
    - HTML::D3 >= 0.20 (radius_range support for scatter bubble charts;
      0.19 added the five new snippet methods).
    - Database::Abstraction >= 0.51 (redis key support).
    - Database::Join >= 0.009.0 (aggregate, limit/offset, dbi_source).

0.011.0	Sun Oct 11 09:20:48 PM EDT 2026
    [ Enhancements ]
    - Added schema browser (GET /tables) for multi-table SQLite databases.
      Opening a SQLite file with more than one internal table now shows a
      card grid listing every table with its columns rather than silently
      opening the first table.  Clicking a card opens that table via the
      existing /open view.  The schema page is inserted into the breadcrumb
      trail so users can navigate back to it.
    - Added ?it=<table> parameter to GET /open, allowing a specific internal
      table to be opened from a multi-table SQLite file.
    - Added sqlite_tables() accessor to DataSource, returning the list of
      internal table names discovered during construction.
    - Added internal_table constructor option to DataSource, letting callers
      request a specific internal SQLite table instead of the auto-detected
      first match.
    - Added data/store.db: sample SQLite database with three joinable tables
      (customer, product, sales) for development and demonstration.
    - Fixed: multi-table symlink for .db-extension SQLite files now uses
      .sql as the symlink extension so Database::Abstraction opens it via
      the DBI/SQLite backend rather than falling through to the CSV reader.
    NOTE: /tables tests currently cover SQLite only.  MySQL, PostgreSQL,
    and other multi-table driver tests will be added in a future release
    once the corresponding Database::Abstraction drivers are available.
    - Server-side pagination for /view/:table and /open.  Both routes now accept
      ?page=N (1-based, default 1) and ?per_page=M (default 200, max 2000).
      The controller uses the N+1 trick: it requests per_page+1 rows via
      LIMIT/OFFSET and treats the extra row as a "has next page" sentinel rather
      than issuing a COUNT(*) query.  This is critical for multi-GB SQLite files
      (e.g. openaddresses.db) where COUNT(*) would block the server for minutes.
      A pagination bar (Prev / current page / Next) is shown when at least two
      pages exist.  All URL parameters (filters, dedup, per_page, etc.) are
      preserved across page navigations.
    - BerkeleyDB files larger than 100 MB now return an informative error page
      instead of causing disk thrashing.  Files whose magic bytes identify them as
      BerkeleyDB but whose DB_File tie() fails (e.g. Berkeley DB version 9 files
      opened with libdb-5.3) would previously fall through to D::A's CSV path,
      causing a full read of the binary file.  DataSource now detects the magic
      bytes in _detect_file_info, refuses files above 100 MB immediately, and
      returns error_unsupported_db for smaller files where tie() fails.
    - Three-level breadcrumb for chart pages.  When a bar, line-graph, pie,
      or heatmap chart is launched from a table view that was itself reached
      from the schema browser (/tables), the chart page now shows the full
      navigation chain (e.g. Home > Store schema > Table view > Chart) rather
      than the previous two-level "Home > Back to table".  The dashboard
      panel forms forward the current page's back_url as back2=/back2_label=
      parameters; the chart controllers promote them to the outer breadcrumb
      level so all four levels are rendered correctly.
    - SQLite hover tooltip on the home-page file picker.  Hovering over a
      database card in the "Choose a database" list now shows a dark popover
      with the file type (e.g. "SQLite database - 3 tables"), last-modified
      date, and file size.  GET /api/stat now returns a table_count integer
      for SQLite-extension files (.sql, .sqlite, .sqlite3, .db); the count
      is omitted for Berkeley DB .db files or other non-SQLite payloads.
      The home-page db-cards now carry data-path attributes so the JS fetch
      can call /api/stat on first mouseenter (lazy, not on page load).

0.010.0	Tue Oct  6 11:29:33 AM EDT 2026
    [ Enhancements ]
    - Added Folder view (GET /folder): browse any data file grouped by the
      letter prefix of a chosen code column (e.g. Order # values like A10,
      CT4, B3).  Records are organised into a two- or three-level folder
      hierarchy -- top level shows distinct first letters (A-Z), clicking a
      letter reveals sub-prefix folders (e.g. CA, CB, CC inside C) and any
      items with that exact prefix, clicking a sub-prefix shows the matching
      records in a table.  A "Folder view..." toolbar button opens a column-
      picker panel identical in style to the chart panels; the code column is
      auto-detected when the panel is opened but the user can override it via
      the dropdown.  Breadcrumb navigation lets the user step back to any
      folder level or return to the source table via "Back to table".
    - upload_file now guards move_to() with eval { ...; 1 } and checks -f
      $dest after the call.  A failed save returns a JSON 500 with the key
      error_upload_save instead of propagating an unhandled exception.
      The orphaned upload subdirectory is removed before the error response
      is sent.  (Uses the eval { ...; 1 } idiom to avoid false positives
      from a stale $@ left by Mojolicious internal dispatch code.)

    - All chart pages (/graph, /pie, /heatmap, /bar) now use responsive SVG
      layout (HTML::D3 0.18 `responsive => 1`): charts scale to the available
      container width so they render correctly on mobile and narrow windows.
    - /bar: added ?max=N parameter -- when N > 0, bars beyond the top N are
      collapsed into a single "Other" bar (HTML::D3 `max_bars`).  Prevents
      unreadable charts from high-cardinality categorical columns.
    - /bar: category-column name is now shown as an axis label below the bars
      (HTML::D3 `x_label`).
    - /pie: added ?scheme= parameter to select the D3 categorical colour
      palette (tableau10, category10, set2, set3, paired; default tableau10).
      Mirrors the existing ?scheme= parameter already on /heatmap.
    - /join: added ?jtype=left|inner|outer parameter to control join semantics.
      `left` (default) keeps all rows from the left table; `inner` returns
      only rows that match in both; `outer` returns all rows from either table.
      Exposed in the "Merge data" panel as a "Which rows to include" dropdown.
    - /join: schema-type-mismatch warnings from Database::Join (e.g. "column
      'score' has type TEXT in left table but INTEGER in right table") are now
      captured and displayed as a yellow notice bar above the data table,
      instead of landing silently in the server error log.
    - DataSource now implements updated() -- proxies to Database::Abstraction's
      updated() or stats the file directly.  This allows Database::Join to
      invalidate its SQLite spill cache when a source file changes on disk.

